  "content": {
    "id": "p132-task45-48-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": null,
    "prompt": {
      "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
      "version": 1,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "p132-stem45-48",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 2,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Determine whether the following functions are odd, even, or neither.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p132-task45-48-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x+\\frac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd.",
          "worked": "The domain is $x\\ne0$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=-x+\\frac{1}{-x}\\\\f(-x)&=-\\left(x+\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p132-task45-48-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=x-\\frac{1}{x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Odd.",
          "worked": "The domain is $x\\ne0$, which is symmetric about $0$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=-x-\\frac{1}{-x}\\\\f(-x)&=-\\left(x-\\frac{1}{x}\\right)\\\\f(-x)&=-f(x).\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, $f$ is odd.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 46
      },
      {
        "id": "p132-task45-48-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{x}{x+1}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither.",
          "worked": "The natural domain is $x\\ne-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{-x}{-x+1}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{x}{x-1}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(2)&=\\frac{2}{3},\\\\f(-2)&=2.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $f(-2)$ equals neither $f(2)$ nor $-f(2)$, so $f$ is neither even nor odd. Its natural domain is also not symmetric about $0$: $1$ is included but $-1$ is excluded.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      },
      {
        "id": "p132-task45-48-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "$f(x)=\\frac{1-x}{1+x}$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Neither.",
          "worked": "The natural domain is $x\\ne-1$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(-x)&=\\frac{1-(-x)}{1+(-x)}\\\\f(-x)&=\\frac{1+x}{1-x}.\\end{align*}$$\n\nFor example,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}f(2)&=-\\frac{1}{3},\\\\f(-2)&=-3.\\end{align*}$$\n\nHere $f(-2)$ equals neither $f(2)$ nor $-f(2)$, so $f$ is neither even nor odd. Its natural domain is also not symmetric about $0$: $1$ is included but $-1$ is excluded.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 54
      }
    ]
  },
